# P&L Variance Summary – FY2025

## Year-over-Year Performance (vs Prior Year)

**Severe Issues:**
- **Operating Profit & Net Profit flipped to losses.** Operating Profit fell RM 4,681,079 (–371%); Net Profit declined RM 3,341,162 (–242%), swinging from profit to loss.
- **Gross Profit collapsed** RM 2,189,240 (–28%), driven by Cost of Sales rising RM 3,815,116 (+5.3%) while Net Sales grew only RM 1,625,876 (+2.0%).
- **Operating Costs surged** RM 2,491,838 (+38%)—material unfavourable variance.

**Margin Deterioration:**
- Gross Margin: 6.9% vs 9.8% prior year (–2.9pp)
- Net Margin: –2.4% vs +1.7% prior year (–4.1pp)

**Offset:** Other Income nearly tripled to RM 1,458,104 (+RM 1,339,917, +1134%), but insufficient to cover operating losses.

## Budget Performance (Approved Budget)

**On Track.** Actual results align nearly perfectly with the approved budget—variances are negligible (–RM 2 to RM 1). All line items within ±0.0% tolerance.

## Overall Picture

**Unfavourable.** The business swung to loss despite modest sales growth. Cost control deteriorated sharply (COGS +5.3%, OpEx +38%), compressing margins below breakeven. Budget compliance is tight, but the budgeted position itself embedded a loss forecast.

